// EXPECT: E0244 — a bare `.` member whose context is not an enum (ADR-0046 §3)
// A *different* problem from having no context at all, so it gets its own wording with the type
// named: "expected `s64`, and a bare `.` member needs an enum". Conflating the two would tell a
// reader to add an annotation they already have.
main :: () {
    n: s64 = .RED;
}
